<title>SINGAPORE: Singatronics gets consent to buy NZ hotel.</title>
<headline>Singatronics gets consent to buy NZ hotel.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singatronics Ltd said on Monday it has incorporated a wholly-owned subsidiary, Glopeak NZ Hotels Pte Ltd (Glopeak NZ), to acquire the Auckland Airport Travelodge in New Zealand.</p>
<p>It said it has obtained approval from the Overseas Investment Commission of New Zealand to acquire the hotel.</p>
<p>Completion of the acquisition will not be later than November 20, 1996. Glopeak NZ has an authorised capital of Singapore $10 million and a paid up capital of S$2.00.</p>
<p>-Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
